Accepted deviation: verse-end placement in a table.

usfm-grammar ends a verse after the last `<cell>` of the row, as a child of
`<row>`. tcdocs puts the end milestone at the last content position instead,
inside the cell: `usfmjsTests/usfmBodyTestD/origin.xml` and
`paratextTests/MissingColumnInTable/origin.xml` both write
`<verse eid="..." /></cell>`, and that is the rule the parser follows
(hardening plan D4; `usfm_parser/tests/verse_ends.rs`). Both shapes are valid
against `usx.rnc`, whose `row` admits `(Verse | TableContent)+`, so this moves
the reference onto tcdocs' shape.

--- origin.xml
+++ origin.xml
@@ -31,8 +31,7 @@
     </row>
     <row style="tr">
       <cell style="tcr1-2" align="end">Total: </cell>
-      <cell style="tcc3" align="center">186,400</cell>
-      <verse eid="NUM 2:3-9"/>
+      <cell style="tcc3" align="center">186,400<verse eid="NUM 2:3-9"/></cell>
     </row>
   </table>
   <chapter eid="NUM 2"/>
